{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>ואושיא</b>: Its root is in the Targum: ונהרסו יסודותיה ויתגלון אושיה (and her foundations were destroyed and her foundations were exposed). And similarly: נפלו אשיותיה (her foundations fell)." "<b>יחיטו</b>: From חוט השני (a line of measurement). Its meaning: they place a line on the foundations for building, like the sense of קו המדה (a measuring line). Or it is from the sense of the Targum: ויתפרו עלה תאנה (and they sewed fig leaves) — וחטיטו and יחיטה having the sense of tying and joining. And the first interpretation is the closer one."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:52.843917612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}